13. Add save and load functionality:
* In the game instance blueprint, create variables to store the player's progress, such as current level, player stats, inventory, etc.
* In the game instance blueprint, create functions to save and load the player's progress to and from a file.
* In the level blueprint, call the save function when the player reaches a checkpoint or when the game is closed.
* In the main menu or other relevant locations, call the load function to restore the player's progress.

Example game instance blueprint code:
```scss
UPROPERTY(EditAnywhere, BlueprintReadWrite, Category = "Save/Load")
FString SaveFileName = "SaveGame";

void SaveGame()
{
    USaveGame* SaveGameInstance = USaveGame::CreateSaveGameInstance();
    SaveGameInstance->CurrentLevel = CurrentLevel;
    SaveGameInstance->PlayerStats = PlayerStats;
    SaveGameInstance->Inventory = Inventory;
    UGameplayStatics::SaveGameToSlot(SaveGameInstance, SaveFileName, 0);
}

void LoadGame()
{
    USaveGame* SaveGameInstance = UGameplayStatics::LoadGameFromSlot(SaveFileName, 0);
    if (SaveGameInstance)
    {
        CurrentLevel = SaveGameInstance->CurrentLevel;
        PlayerStats = SaveGameInstance->PlayerStats;
        Inventory = SaveGameInstance->Inventory;
    }
}
```
